From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phone-rpc: preserve volatile namespace failure semantics

Offline regressions reproduce snapshot resurrection after rename and namespace
exhaustion from missing-source renames. Keep bounded tombstones so removed names
cannot silently reappear from the immutable snapshot. Reserve a tombstone slot
before committing rename, retain source handles, and refuse table exhaustion or
busy destinations without changing prior bytes or names.

Allocate the index when append creates a missing file; previously that path used
an uninitialized index. Normalize VFS negative errno, check handle availability
before seeding, roll back a failed new seed, and use the signed IDL seek offset.
The RAM namespace and byte/handle caps remain unchanged. No host writes are added.

Tests exercise the actual wire dispatcher, seeded rename/read/restore, missing
append creation, signed seek, missing-name floods, ENOMEM and full-table refusal.
This is offline userspace correctness evidence, not sensor-stream qualification.

